{"answer":"Your next week starts with three easy walks, progressing from 20 to 30 minutes. This rebuilds endurance from your usual walking base (typically 16 minutes) without jumping straight to running; your recent sessions were sparse and your latest readiness was moderate. [47d15557-e8] [47d15557-e13]

Keep the walks comfortably conversational. This is a deliberately modest 75-minute start, not an attempt to reach the general 150–300-minute weekly target immediately. [47d15557-e39] Stop if pain, dizziness, unusual breathlessness, chest discomfort, or palpitations occur; seek medical care urgently for chest symptoms, fainting, severe dizziness, breathlessness at rest, or palpitations.

Reassess before progressing next week, especially if sleep or recovery changes.","outcome":"answer","reason":"Plan is based on the person’s stated goal, availability, preferences and current state, plus recent training, recovery and sleep records."}

